// Native interlayer DMI couples across a nonmagnetic spacer gap (z-column scan).
// Magnetic layers at z=0 (region 100) and z=2 (region 101); the cell at z=1 is
// empty (Msat=0). The partner is found across the gap, and the antisymmetric
// stacking sign is preserved (region 100 sees its partner above, region 101
// below), so the fields match the adjacent case.
// D = -2e-3 J/m2, Msat = 1e6 A/m, dz = 0.9e-9 m  ->  |D/(Msat*dz)| = 2.22222 T.
SetGridSize(16, 16, 3)
SetCellSize(2e-9, 2e-9, 0.9e-9)
setgeom(layer(0).add(layer(2)))
Msat = 1.0e6
defregion(100, layer(0))
defregion(101, layer(2))
ext_InterlayerDMI(100, 101, -2e-3)
m.setRegion(100, uniform(1, 0, 0))
m.setRegion(101, uniform(0, 1, 0))
Run(0)
ExpectV("B_idmi across spacer (region 100)", B_idmi.Region(100).Average(), vector(2.22222, 0, 0), 1e-3)
ExpectV("B_idmi across spacer (region 101)", B_idmi.Region(101).Average(), vector(0, 2.22222, 0), 1e-3)
